Add a WebAssembly host, wasm32-wasi, and fix two calls that only work where
a call's arguments are not checked against its callee.

The host is 32-bit and little-endian like the i386, so a wide integer of 32
bits keeps what the compiler generates the same as on any other host.

insn_gen_function was declared variadic, but its entries, gen_movsi and the
rest, are not: on WebAssembly a variadic call passes its variable arguments
through a pointer, so the callee read that pointer as its second operand. It
is declared without a prototype instead, as genoutput already defines it.

calls.c passes call and call_value as many operands as any target's take,
more than MIPS's do, which a WebAssembly direct call cannot do. It calls
them through a pointer, which the build then makes tolerant of the count.

WASI has no processes, so pexecute, by which the driver runs cpp0, cc1, as
and collect2, writes each command to the file GCC_WASI_PLAN names instead,
for mipsel-ecoff-gcc to run under a WASI runtime, and reports success.

